from pathlib import Path
import json,base64
P=Path(__file__).parent;load=lambda n:json.loads((P/n).read_text());m=load('texture-review-manifest.json');stats=load('runtime-measurements.json');primary=load('PRIMARY-SOURCE-MANIFEST.json');uri=lambda n:'data:image/png;base64,'+base64.b64encode((P/n).read_bytes()).decode()
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"><title>Bushtit — small-size closure study</title><style>body{font:16px system-ui;margin:24px;max-width:1150px;background:#ece7d8;color:#24372b}h1{font-size:24px}.row{display:flex;gap:28px;flex-wrap:wrap}.card{padding:18px;border:1px solid #b7b59f;border-radius:8px}.dark{background:#17251f;color:#edf0dc}.light{background:#e5e0cd}canvas,img{image-rendering:pixelated}canvas{width:64px;height:64px}button{padding:7px;margin:5px}pre{font-size:12px;white-space:pre-wrap}#status{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}</style></head><body><h1>Bushtit: one new closed-eye study/candidate</h1><p>One native closure and the exact unchanged existing awake drawing. No new neutral/look, rigged body motion or app binding. Independent review must decide whether the eye change reads at this small size; unreadable/distracting closure stays a study rather than an implemented blink.</p><p>Existing96²source output displays on a64CSS-pixel world canvas atdensity1.5. The actual bird is only28–28.667world pixels wide and18high. Judge the primary light/dark playback at that size before enlargement.</p><button id="play">Play / restart</button><button id="pause">Pause</button><button id="open">Hold existing open</button><button id="closed">Hold new closed</button><label><input id="overlay" type="checkbox">Root/contact overlay</label><p id="status"></p><div class="row"><div class="card light"><p>Actual world size — light</p><canvas id="light" width="96" height="96"></canvas></div><div class="card dark"><p>Actual world size — dark</p><canvas id="dark" width="96" height="96"></canvas></div><div class="card light"><p>4x output inspection</p><canvas id="zoom" width="96" height="96" style="width:384px;height:384px"></canvas></div></div><p>30Hz loop:open60ticks,closed3ticks,open27ticks (3seconds;100msclosure). Root remains[57,75]. Both actual lower-foot mask boundaries are75output px; centroid difference0.0774output px (~0.0516world), mask Hausdorff1px. Shared contact pixels[56,73],[58,73] remain positive-alpha. This is technical registration, not tracked anatomical toe approval.</p><p>Native1254²canvas→1024²whole-canvas nearest→96²nearest. No translation, pose fit, body warp, source painting, alpha cleanup or palette quantization. Native edit redrew outside the eye: silhouette IoU0.957071 and visible outside-eye mean RGB difference15.8106/255. These are diagnostics rather than a universal pixel-equality gate. Tiny eye-read and texture flicker remain review questions.</p><img style="max-width:100%;height:auto" src="__CONTACTS__"><details><summary>Exact-timing standalone source APNG</summary><img width="96" height="96" style="width:64px;height:64px" src="__APNG_URI__"></details><details><summary>Exact source/intake/mapping/measurements</summary><pre>__METADATA__</pre></details><script>const manifest=__MANIFEST__,stats=__STATS__,urls=__URLS__;const ims={};let tick=0,playing=false,start=0;const canvases=['light','dark','zoom'].map(id=>document.getElementById(id));function state(){const phase=tick>=60&&tick<63?'closed':'open';return{tick,phase,outputFrameId:phase==='open'?__OPENID__:__CLOSEDID__,rootOutputXY:[57,75],density:1.5,appBound:false}}function draw(t){tick=((Math.floor(t)%90)+90)%90;const s=state();for(const c of canvases){const ctx=c.getContext('2d');ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled=false;ctx.fillStyle=c.id==='dark'?'#17251f':'#e5e0cd';ctx.fillRect(0,0,96,96);ctx.drawImage(ims[s.phase],0,0);if(document.getElementById('overlay').checked){ctx.fillStyle='#07b876';for(const a of manifest.frames[0].contacts)ctx.fillRect(a.x-1,a.y-1,2,2);ctx.strokeStyle='#d77d20';ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(54,75);ctx.lineTo(60,75);ctx.moveTo(57,72);ctx.lineTo(57,78);ctx.stroke()}}document.getElementById('status').textContent=`Tick ${tick}/89 • ${s.phase} • density1.5 • fixedroot[57,75]`;return s}function raf(now){if(playing)draw((now-start)*30/1000);requestAnimationFrame(raf)}function play(){start=performance.now();playing=true;draw(0)}document.getElementById('play').onclick=play;document.getElementById('pause').onclick=()=>playing=false;document.getElementById('open').onclick=()=>{playing=false;draw(0)};document.getElementById('closed').onclick=()=>{playing=false;draw(60)};document.getElementById('overlay').onchange=()=>draw(tick);window.BUSHTIT_REVIEW={ready:false,seek:t=>{playing=false;return draw(t)},getState:state,play,pause:()=>playing=false,manifest,stats};Promise.all(Object.entries(urls).map(([name,url])=>new Promise((resolve,reject)=>{const im=new Image();im.onload=()=>{ims[name]=im;resolve()};im.onerror=reject;im.src=url}))).then(()=>{window.BUSHTIT_REVIEW.ready=true;draw(0);requestAnimationFrame(raf)});</script></body></html>'''
html=html.replace('__CONTACTS__',uri('normal-light-dark-eye-feet.png')).replace('__APNG_URI__',uri('blink.apng')).replace('__METADATA__',json.dumps({'source':primary,'intake':m,'mapping':load('frame-to-action-map.json'),'measurements':stats},indent=2)).replace('__MANIFEST__',json.dumps(m)).replace('__STATS__',json.dumps(stats)).replace('__URLS__',json.dumps({'open':uri('open96.png'),'closed':uri('closed96.png')})).replace('__OPENID__',json.dumps(primary['reusedFrames'][0]['outputFrameId'])).replace('__CLOSEDID__',json.dumps(primary['frames'][0]['outputFrameId']));(P/'review.html').write_text(html)
